APPLICATION ACK ΓÇö 2026-08-14

`APPLICATION_ACK = ACCEPTED`

The FSATS Application workstream reviewed the Owner-directed future-stage FCR lifecycle rule against the current Application FCR handling model and found no concrete incompatibility.

Application adopts the same operating semantics going forward:
- implementation-required future Foundation work remains `Waiting On: FOUNDATION` until the Foundation-owned code and governed verification/evidence are complete;
- once the Foundation-owned portion is implemented and verified, a mixed Foundation/Application FCR hands off to `Waiting On: APPLICATION` until Application-owned implementation/binding/verification is complete;
- design/planning/assignment/reaching a future Stage/WP does not satisfy implementation-required closure;
- `Waiting On: NONE` is not used merely because the next action belongs to a future Stage/WP;
- `Target Foundation Stage/WP` and `Review Trigger` remain explicit and must not fabricate placement or authority;
- historical comments/evidence remain preserved;
- FCR state never grants implementation/runtime authority by itself.

No current FSATS governance conflict was identified.

`APPLICATION_ACK_RESULT = ACCEPTED / SYNCHRONIZED_FOR_FUTURE_FCR_LIFECYCLE`

HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=FOUNDATION; Next Required Action=Foundation shall consume this Application ACK together with the Shared Web ACK, synchronize the shared FCR operating protocol/current headers as planned, and disposition this governance-synchronization FCR.; Target Foundation Stage/WP=N/A ΓÇö cross-workstream FCR governance synchronization; Review Trigger=Foundation synchronization/disposition after both requested ACKs are reviewed.
